    "short_description": "The Central Norway Regional Health Authority (Helse Midt-Norge RHF) is a state-owned enterprise responsible for operating hospitals and providing specialist health services in the central Norwegian counties of Trøndelag and Møre og Romsdal. Established between 2001 and 2002, it is based in Stjørdal and employs around 15,000 people.\n\nThe authority operates nine hospitals across five health trusts, offering a range of services including physical health care, mental health care, and substance abuse treatment. It also provides emergency services, hospital pharmacies, and medical testing through its laboratories. The Central Norway Regional Health Authority serves the residents of its region, focusing on patients, their families, healthcare personnel, and researchers. It is committed to patient treatment, education, and supporting medical research.",
